ange of $y,$ note that $t+2\\ge 3$ for all $t\\ge 1.$ Consequently, $y=t+2\\ge 3.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $x\\le 2$ and $y\\ge 3.$" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381286 13194139536057 true] [17592186381285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381287 13194139536057 true] [17592186381285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381288 13194139536057 true] [17592186381285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381289 13194139536057 true] [17592186381285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381290 13194139536057 true] [17592186381285 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536057 true] [17592186381285 1041 "selection" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381285 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381288 13194139536057 true] [17592186381285 1110 #uuid "e86aca44-c7c0-5583-9c31-3cd0b8f79e83" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381286 1034 "x\\le -3,\\,y\\ge 2" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381286 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536057 true] [17592186381286 1111 #uuid "bf36275d-b1ce-5fa5-baac-0c8f5a6f9b0f" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381287 1034 "x\\le 2,\\,y\\ge -3" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381287 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536057 true] [17592186381287 1111 #uuid "6a9d2a05-16ca-5a5a-8adc-be64a53fb485" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381288 1034 "x\\le 2,\\,y\\ge 3" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381288 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536057 true] [17592186381288 1111 #uuid "d469f98d-b407-5209-a1c7-c69ae82764ea" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381289 1034 "x\\ge -1,\\,y\\ge 3" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536057 true] [17592186381289 1111 #uuid "32e1787a-9224-57f6-aac6-3f2e9582bb66" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381290 1034 "x\\ge 3,\\,y\\le -2" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381290 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536057 true] [17592186381290 1111 #uuid "6d462a95-0202-5902-85b9-5c8e6d47059e" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381291 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381292 13194139536057 true] [17592186381291 1089 "q-123775" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381291 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536057 true] [17592186381291 1100 "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381291 1113 #uuid "df6cb91b-a536-5526-9dd6-80b470cc8a61" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381291 1145 "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\le \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -1+3 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3\\le 1+3 \\\\ 2 & \\le y\\le 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $2\\le y\\le 4.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $-\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2}$ and $2\\le y\\le 4.$" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381292 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381293 13194139536057 true] [17592186381292 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381294 13194139536057 true] [17592186381292 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381295 13194139536057 true] [17592186381292 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381296 13194139536057 true] [17592186381292 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381297 13194139536057 true] [17592186381292 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536057 true] [17592186381292 1041 "selection" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381292 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381296 13194139536057 true] [17592186381292 1110 #uuid "d74e8d49-0a7c-5237-b08b-b742646e39bb" 13194139536057 true] [17592186381293 1034 "-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-4\\le y\\le -2" 13194139536057 true] [1759218638